\[ f(n) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl} 
6 & \text{ if } n \text{ is a multiple of 2 and 3 (i.e., 6)}, \\ 
2 & \text{ if } n \text{ is only a multiple of 2 (i.e., 2, 4, 6)}, \\ 
0 & \text{ if } n \text{ is not a multiple of 2 (i.e., 1, 3, 5)}. 
\end{array}
\right.\]

Next, we calculate the points for each roll based on this function. Allie's rolls are 5, 4, 1, and 2, so her points are \(0, 2, 0, 2\). Betty's rolls are 6, 3, 3, and 2, so her points are \(6, 0, 0, 2\).

The total points for Allie are \(0 + 2 + 0 + 2 = 4\). The total points for Betty are \(6 + 0 + 0 + 2 = 8\). The product of their total points is \(4 \times 8 = 32\).</think> <answer>32</answer>
